The general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present, as amended on 2 May 2026[[cite:obs-ff113a3b1875159208e86e806097711614f91d4c "the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present."]]. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. The bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present[[cite:obs-8246a9ae98ae77d9006c2b94a720237df29feaf1 "The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present."]].